Controller function **1320** uses separate channel select lines **23\(a\), 23\(b\)** and **23\(c\)** to control left video switch **21\(a\),** right video switch **21\(b\)** and peripheral switch respectively.

[0430] For example in this figure, assuming that display **2\(a\)** and **2\(b\)** are different type:

[0431] Host **6\(a\)** is reading right DPPEM device **10\(ab\)** reflecting display **2\(b\)** EDID;

[0432] Host **6\(b\)** is reading right DPPEM device **10\(bb\)** reflecting display **2\(b\)** EDID;

[0433] Host **6\(c\)** is reading left DPPEM device **10\(ca\)** reflecting display **2\(a\)** EDID;

[0434] Host **6\(d\)** is reading right DPPEM device **10\(db\)** reflecting display **2\(b\)** EDID;

[0435] In this figure, left display **2\(a\)** is connected to first host **6\(c\)** and right display is connected to second host **6\(d\)**. Controller function **1320** control the four EDID right-left select switches **31\(a\), 31\(b\), 31\(c\)** and **31\(d\)**. The control algorithm in controller function **1320** may reduce display changes for attached hosts by leaving last source selected for non-selected hosts. In this figure the two non-selected hosts **6\(a\)** and **6\(b\)** are switched to the right DPPEM devices **10\(ab\)** and **10\(bb\)** respectively.

[0436] FIG. 23 illustrates a more detailed block diagram of the controller function **1320** and four DPPEM **10\(aa\)** to **10\(bb\)** of the Secure KVM **1305** shown in FIGS. 20 to 22 above. In this figure three of the four DPPEM devices are further connected to KVM Mode select line **22** to enable address change in Write Mode.

[0437] During Normal Mode when KVM Mode select line **22** is in logic 0 state, all four DPPEM device address lines are in logic 0 and therefore devices may be properly read at 00h address by hosts **6**. As Secure KVM **1305** changes mode to Write Mode, KVM Mode select line **22** is in logic1 state forcing the three DPPEM devices **10\(ab\)** to **10\(bb\)
